From 06870345eaed75747820402c4c95e95ece18658a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Payton <brandon@happycode.net>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 00:36:39 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] regexp/syntax: Compile deep expressions without
 recursion

Simplification of counted repetitions can produce expressions that exhaust
WebAssembly engines' native call stacks even though Go's goroutine stack
can grow. Compile with an explicit stack, preserving instruction emission,
patching order and capture priority in one traversal implementation shared
by all platforms.

Add deep concatenation and capture regression tests, including shared
subtrees. Existing regexp/syntax and regexp tests pass on darwin/arm64.
An evaluation-only recursive oracle produces identical complete programs
for 2,022 fixed and generated expressions. The previously overflowing URL
patterns pass both WASI architectures on Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.

This is a candidate for upstream evaluation. Compilation-time and
allocation measurements remain pending; default package consumers have
not switched to this branch.

